# Task 16 — SDL2 CLUU Video, Software-Renderer, and Events Backends

## Summary

Implemented five logical video files for the SDL2 CLUU backend (spec §3.6):
displayd surface protocol for pixel output, compositor input-forward for
keyboard events, software renderer only (no accelerated renderer advertised).

## Files Created

- `userspace/sdl2/SDL2-2.30.0/src/video/cluu/SDL_cluuvideo.h`
  — Shared declarations: CLUU protocol constants, ProcessInfo layout
  (#[repr(C)] at 0x7fe00100), IPC Message struct (56 bytes), inline syscall
  helpers (x86_64 SYSCALL with explicit r10/r8/r9 register constraints),
  IPC wrapper functions (send/call/recv_any/invoke), per-window and
  per-device driver data structs.

- `userspace/sdl2/SDL2-2.30.0/src/video/cluu/SDL_cluuvideo.c`
  — Bootstrap (CLUU_bootstrap), CreateDevice, VideoInit (queries displayd
  OUTPUT_INFO for screen dimensions, creates IPC endpoint for input events,
  creates registry control endpoint, subscribes to compositor:client for
  keyboard input), VideoQuit. CLUU_Available() only activates when
  SDL_VIDEODRIVER=cluu hint is set — avoids touching unmapped ProcessInfo
  memory on non-CLUU hosts.

- `userspace/sdl2/SDL2-2.30.0/src/video/cluu/SDL_cluuwindow.c`
  — CreateSDLWindow: creates displayd surface (SurfaceCreate + SetGeometry,
  centered for windowed, top-left for fullscreen), registers compositor
  window (WinRegister) for keyboard input forwarding. DestroyWindow:
  destroys displayd surface + compositor window. ShowWindow/HideWindow/
  RaiseWindow: state tracking. SetWindowFullscreen: composite fallback
  (moves surface to 0,0, no VT theft, no scanout promotion).

- `userspace/sdl2/SDL2-2.30.0/src/video/cluu/SDL_cluuframebuffer.c`
  — CreateWindowFramebuffer: allocates kernel frame token
  (invoke FrameAllocate), maps it into process address space at 0xD2000000
  (invoke SpaceMapRange with MAP_FRAME_TOKEN flag), returns mapped pointer
  as SDL framebuffer (software renderer writes directly to frame token
  memory). UpdateWindowFramebuffer: sends BUFFER_COMMIT to displayd with
  frame token and damage rects (clipped to surface bounds, capped at 8
  rects, bounding-box fallback for >8). DestroyWindowFramebuffer: unmaps
  and frees frame token.

- `userspace/sdl2/SDL2-2.30.0/src/video/cluu/SDL_cluuevents.c`
  — PumpEvents: polls input endpoint (non-blocking) for COMP_INPUT_FORWARD
  messages from compositor. Converts PS/2 set-2 scancodes to SDL scancodes
  (USB HID) via lookup table covering all main keys (letters, digits,
  function keys, arrows, modifiers, keypad). Kind 99 → SDL_SendQuit.
  Kind 0/1 → SDL_SendKeyboardKey(SDL_PRESSED/SDL_RELEASED). Also pumps
  registry control endpoint for late grant delivery.

