## Architecture

The C backend talks to displayd and the compositor via raw CLUU kernel
syscalls (inline assembly). No Rust libcluu linkage is needed at the C
level — ProcessInfo and Message are #[repr(C)] and their memory layout
is stable.

### Pixel output path
  SDL software renderer → mapped frame token memory (0xD2000000)
  → UpdateWindowFramebuffer → BUFFER_COMMIT IPC to displayd
  → displayd maps frame token, copies pixels to surface buffer, composites

### Input path
  kbd driver → compositor → COMP_INPUT_FORWARD → our IPC endpoint
  → PumpEvents → SDL_SendKeyboardKey / SDL_SendQuit

### Fullscreen
  Composite fallback only. Surface moves to (0,0). No VT theft, no
  scanout promotion. SDL_WINDOW_FULLSCREEN flag is honored by repositioning
  the displayd surface — the compositor composites it.

### Renderer
  Software renderer only (SDL_VIDEO_RENDER_SW). No SDL_RENDERER_ACCELERATED
  is advertised. SDL_CreateRenderer with ACCELERATED flag falls back to
  software automatically (SDL's built-in behavior).

