### Runtime execution
The probe binary is a CLUU userspace ELF that links cleanly with zero
undefined symbols. Executing the 100-cycle loop requires the CLUU kernel
runtime (CLUU crt0 + libcluu_syscalls make syscalls to the CLUU kernel,
not to the host Linux kernel). Running it on the host produces a segfault
— this is expected and is the same behavior as T14 (documented in
.omo/evidence/task-14-cluu-multimedia-stack.txt).

The CLUU backend activates only when SDL_VIDEODRIVER=cluu is set. Without
the hint, the dummy backend is used (for host tests / headless paths).
On CLUU, the application or init system sets the hint before SDL_Init.

